.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS-PLAY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings-play - Replay a recording in this terminal


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings play <recording-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Replay one recording in this terminal at its recorded pace. --speed scales the pace and
--idle-limit caps any pause between frames (default 2s); both must be positive. The replay
is audited and needs your ENV vault unlocked; if it is locked the command says to run
pb env unlock. --archive replays the archived copy in the team bucket instead of asking the
machine, which is useful when the machine is offline.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--archive\fP[=false]
	replay the copy in the team bucket instead of asking the machine

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for play

.PP
\fB--idle-limit\fP=2s
	longest pause between frames

.PP
\fB--speed\fP=1
	playback speed


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings play rec_abc123
  pb recordings play rec_abc123 --speed 2 --idle-limit 1s
  pb recordings play rec_abc123 --archive
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recordings(1)\fP
